#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114966 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115386 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ac33006-2d6d-5ee2-9749-a1f3dea17869" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Limit of a Vector Function"}] :question/id #uuid "4e4541ff-5c48-5300-ac29-e48111fee506" :question/math-academy-id "e-2394" :question/problem "Calculate  $\\lim\\limits_{t \\to 0} \\mathbf{f}(t),$ given that \n\n$$\n\\mathbf f (t) = \\dfrac{1- e^{t}}{\\sin t} \\ \\mathbf {i}+ \\dfrac{\\sin t}{t+t^2} \\ \\mathbf {j} + \\dfrac{ e^{t} - e^{-t}}{\\sin t} \\ \\mathbf {k}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the limit of our vector function, we compute the limit of each component individually:\n\n$$\n\\lim_{t \\to 0}\\mathbf f(t) = \\left(\\lim_{t \\to 0} \\dfrac{1-e^t}{\\sin t}\\right)\\,\\mathbf i + \\left( \\lim_{t \\to 0} \\dfrac{\\sin t}{t+t^2}\\right)\\,\\mathbf j + \\left( \\lim_{t \\to 0} \\dfrac{e^t-e^{-t}}{\\sin t} \\right)\\,\\mathbf k\n$$\n\nNow, we find the limits one-by-one.\n\n- The first component can be found using L'Hopital's Rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{1-{e}^{t}}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} & ={lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{{(1-{e}^{t})}^{′}}{{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{-{e}^{t}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{-{e}^{0}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡0} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{1} \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second component can be found using a special limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{t+{t}^{2}} & ={lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{t(t+1)} \\\\  & =({lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{1}{t+1})\\cdot ({lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{t}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{0+1})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third component can be found using L'Hopital's Rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{t}-{e}^{-t}}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} & ={lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{{({e}^{t}-{e}^{-t})}^{′}}{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{t}+{e}^{-t}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{0}+{e}^{-0}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+1}{1} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\lim\\limits_{t \\to 0}\\mathbf f(t) = -\\mathbf i + \\mathbf j +2\\,\\mathbf k.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114967 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115387 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "610e605b-30f6-574b-b149-3717cfd4d72a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Limit of the Magnitude of a Vector Function"}] :question/id #uuid "b5f3f5c9-3d28-5fee-8d67-d49d743ae474" :question/math-academy-id "e-2395" :question/problem "Calculate $\\lim\\limits_{t \\to \\infty} \\| \\mathbf f(t) \\|$ if $\\mathbf f(t)  = \\left\\langle t^{-1}, \\: \\left(1+\\dfrac{3}{t}\\right)^t, \\: \\dfrac{t^2}{1-t^2} \\right\\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the limit of our vector function, we compute the limit of each component individually:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }f(t) & =⟨{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }{t}^{-1},\\,{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{3}{t})}^{t},\\,{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }\\frac{{t}^{2}}{1-{t}^{2}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the limits one-by-one.\n\n- For the first component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }{t}^{-1} & ={lim}_{t\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{t}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second component can be found using a special limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{3}{t})}^{t} & ={lim}_{t\\to \\infty }{[{(1+\\frac{1}{t/3})}^{t/3}]}^{3} \\\\  & ={[{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{t/3})}^{t/3}]}^{3} \\\\  & =[\\,e\\,]^{3} \\\\  & ={e}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the third component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }\\frac{{t}^{2}}{1-{t}^{2}} & ={lim}_{t\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}-1}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\lim\\limits_{t \\to \\infty}\\mathbf f(t) = \\left\\langle 0, \\: e^3, \\: -1\\right\\rangle.\n$$\n\nFinally, the limit of $\\left\\| \\mathbf f(t) \\right\\|$ as $t$ approaches $\\infty$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }‖f(t)‖ & =‖{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }f(t)‖ \\\\  & =‖⟨0,\\,{e}^{3},\\,-1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+({e}^{3})^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{6}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114968 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115388 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "68832b12-c34c-5770-9566-fc2fa915d005" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Limit of a Sum of Vector Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "c2055711-815d-5385-8f31-19cc81f20698" :question/math-academy-id "e-2396" :question/problem "Find $\\displaystyle \\lim_{t \\to 0} \\big[ \\mathbf f(t) - 2 \\mathbf g(t) \\big]$ given that $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)$ are defined as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ {e}^{t} \\\\ t\\end{bmatrix},\\,g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2t\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the limit of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}{lim}_{t\\to 0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 0}{e}^{t} \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 0}t\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡0 \\\\ {e}^{0} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 0}g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}{lim}_{t\\to 0}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 0}1 \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 0}2t\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use properties of limits to calculate the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}[f(t)-2g(t)] & ={lim}_{t\\to 0}f(t)-2{lim}_{t\\to 0}g(t) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114969 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115389 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb0058fd-f8c2-5f5d-bd48-f497537622dd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Limit of a Product of Vector Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "53cccd72-1595-5316-8162-731103c2da28" :question/math-academy-id "e-2397" :question/problem "Find $\\displaystyle \\lim_{t \\to 2} \\left[\\mathbf f(t) \\cdot \\mathbf g(t)\\right]$ given that $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)$ are defined as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,i+t\\,j+{t}^{2}\\,k \\\\ g(t) & =(2-t)\\,i+\\frac{6}{t}\\,j-4\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the limit of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 2}f(t) & =({lim}_{t\\to 2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)\\,i+({lim}_{t\\to 2}t)\\,j+({lim}_{t\\to 2}{t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)\\,i+2\\,j+{2}^{2}\\,k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,i+2\\,j+4\\,k, \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 2}g(t) & =({lim}_{t\\to 2}(2-t))\\,i+({lim}_{t\\to 2}\\frac{6}{t})\\,j+({lim}_{t\\to 2}(-4))\\,k \\\\  & =(2-2)\\,i+\\frac{6}{2}\\,j+(-4)\\,k \\\\  & =0\\,i+3\\,j-4\\,k \\\\  & =3\\,j-4\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use properties of limits to calculate the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 2}[f(t)\\cdot g(t)] & ={lim}_{t\\to 2}f(t)\\cdot {lim}_{t\\to 2}g(t) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,i+2\\,j+4\\,k)\\cdot (3\\,j-4\\,k) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 3+4\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =-10\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563714 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115386 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ac33006-2d6d-5ee2-9749-a1f3dea17869" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Limit of a Vector Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b00c5fc-121b-578b-aae9-3de39a26ee79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,i+j+3\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563006} {:answer/id #uuid "62b08d41-0939-5d9c-8e45-e87ba0e15a2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+2\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563172} {:answer/id #uuid "e79ab410-d634-5646-bfb0-ece61ffb440f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "j+4\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563460} {:answer/id #uuid "f6be0740-a62e-58fd-9a09-75e30cd955e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+4\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563495} {:answer/id #uuid "f827c61f-b0c2-5eb2-aa99-dfd1a0790afa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,i-j+4\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563498}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e79ab410-d634-5646-bfb0-ece61ffb440f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "j+4\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563460} :answer-field/id #uuid "8276de71-5ba4-56fb-966c-b20d81bdc55e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563583}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8a16b58b-bb85-5099-b69a-a964f563de29" :question/math-academy-id "q-127725" :question/problem "Find the limit ${lim}_{t\\to 0}f(t),$ if $f(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+(t+2)^{2}\\,k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{t\\to 0}f(t)=({lim}_{t\\to 0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)i+({lim}_{t\\to 0}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)j+({lim}_{t\\to 0}(t+2)^{2})k.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the limits one-by-one.\n\n- For the first component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}\\operatorname{cos}⁡0=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the third component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}\\,(t+2)^{2} & =(0+2)^{2}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{t\\to 0}f(t)=j+4\\,k.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563661 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115386 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ac33006-2d6d-5ee2-9749-a1f3dea17869" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Limit of a Vector Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17bfca3e-307e-5781-bcef-233b9377631e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,2,\\frac{3}{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562998} {:answer/id #uuid "2fbe2ff0-d6cc-58ae-957f-7ee6c2b531e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\frac{3}{4},1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563053} {:answer/id #uuid "502c5e1c-390a-5709-91ed-47d4584cce04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,2,\\frac{1}{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563129} {:answer/id #uuid "87d95073-b451-52be-860e-7824c423abac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{3}{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563248} {:answer/id #uuid "8def5c03-9698-5566-8421-3e7a87a68af7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,0,\\frac{3}{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563266}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17bfca3e-307e-5781-bcef-233b9377631e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,2,\\frac{3}{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562998} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fb29db3-ac82-5b56-ae72-c2f44640f27f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563594}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2c409cd1-fe1f-5e01-a403-dbc5d06f9573" :question/math-academy-id "q-127734" :question/problem "Calculate ${lim}_{t\\to 2}f(t),$ if $f(t)=⟨{e}^{t-2},\\,\\sqrt{6-t},\\,\\frac{3}{t+2}⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{t\\to 2}f(t)=⟨{lim}_{t\\to 2}{e}^{t-2},\\,{lim}_{t\\to 2}\\sqrt{6-t},\\,{lim}_{t\\to 2}\\frac{3}{t+2}⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the limits one by one.\n\n- For the first component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 2}{e}^{t-2} & ={e}^{2-2} \\\\  & ={e}^{0} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 2}\\sqrt{6-t} & =\\sqrt{6-2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the third component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 2}\\frac{3}{t+2} & =\\frac{3}{2+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{t\\to 2}f(t)=⟨1,2,\\frac{3}{4}⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563738 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115386 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ac33006-2d6d-5ee2-9749-a1f3dea17869" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Limit of a Vector Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07b010d6-1bf1-5424-be3f-473792bd873e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,8,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562954} {:answer/id #uuid "21e427fa-5df8-5fc8-ab03-e130781f6c1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,5,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563021} {:answer/id #uuid "2f82b2ed-bb1e-5c79-9b96-dcd0e6db45e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-3,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563051} {:answer/id #uuid "be42811a-f4bf-56a2-abb8-9899f924d1af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,3,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563364} {:answer/id #uuid "c3e4948e-79e5-5d75-89f0-87fe6fc505da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,3,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be42811a-f4bf-56a2-abb8-9899f924d1af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,3,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563364} :answer-field/id #uuid "84e8b7b2-23ed-5a0a-99f0-5172dcf54f18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563586}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d22af4f5-52e4-5523-b72f-519be01c5f87" :question/math-academy-id "q-130202" :question/problem "Calculate ${lim}_{s\\to 2}f(s)$, if $f(s)=⟨\\frac{5}{{e}^{s-2}},\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4-2s),\\,{s}^{3}-5⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{s\\to 2}f(s)=⟨{lim}_{s\\to 2}\\frac{5}{{e}^{s-2}},\\,{lim}_{s\\to 2}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4-2s),\\,{lim}_{s\\to 2}\\,({s}^{3}-5)⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the limits one by one.\n\n- For the first component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 2}\\frac{5}{{e}^{s-2}} & =\\frac{5}{{e}^{2-2}}=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the first component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 2}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4-2s) & =3{lim}_{s\\to 2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4-2s) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4-2\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡0 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the third component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 2}\\,({s}^{3}-5) & ={2}^{3}-5=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{s\\to 2}f(s)=⟨5,3,3⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563754 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115386 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ac33006-2d6d-5ee2-9749-a1f3dea17869" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Limit of a Vector Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1238dba3-92d9-5c65-88f6-15a8db8223ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562982} {:answer/id #uuid "14ae2243-a263-5f30-bc1e-4f040a2ebd84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562988} {:answer/id #uuid "526b9721-1d50-5045-be99-28fbfc65b137" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563132} {:answer/id #uuid "8118547b-32c2-5862-a697-3f257283fb92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563229} {:answer/id #uuid "b92debbe-4905-5cf5-ac7e-54ae5dd148f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563351}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b92debbe-4905-5cf5-ac7e-54ae5dd148f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563351} :answer-field/id #uuid "934d475b-f1bc-5ebd-a7fa-3293dabf3b69" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563596}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e7a9644a-6597-5c1c-8581-2dcd08c08372" :question/math-academy-id "q-130205" :question/problem "Calculate ${lim}_{s\\to 1}f(s),$ if $f(s)=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5-s} \\\\ \\frac{{e}^{1-s}}{s} \\\\ (1+5s)^{1-s}\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{s\\to 1}f(s)=[\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 1}\\sqrt{5-s} \\\\ {lim}_{s\\to 1}\\frac{{e}^{1-s}}{s} \\\\ {lim}_{s\\to 1}\\,(1+5s)^{1/(2s)}.\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we find the limits one by one.\n\n- For the first component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 1}\\sqrt{5-s} & =\\sqrt{5-1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 1}\\frac{{e}^{1-s}}{s}=\\frac{{e}^{1-1}}{1}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the third component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 1}\\,(1+5s)^{1-s} & =(1+5\\cdot 1)^{1-1} \\\\  & ={6}^{0} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{s\\to 1}f(s)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563693 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115387 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "610e605b-30f6-574b-b149-3717cfd4d72a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Limit of the Magnitude of a Vector Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a396a767-5b66-5bd2-8cc1-072e21a93b90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563315} {:answer/id #uuid "a7554a6f-0aea-5a5a-9c28-e56e4d345ff6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563324} {:answer/id #uuid "b5d6b95a-ada9-5465-b9fb-5a72172eca4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563346} {:answer/id #uuid "e4fb20f9-8aa7-571a-9473-7ce075be4841" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563450} {:answer/id #uuid "f06540a4-643a-5da8-a809-4757dd6f0a17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563481}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5d6b95a-ada9-5465-b9fb-5a72172eca4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563346} :answer-field/id #uuid "8dbde469-aa7e-5bcb-a66c-2dae3c6fa5e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563591}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6199f517-7214-5d4f-b510-e7e4d600a748" :question/math-academy-id "q-130211" :question/problem "Calculate ${lim}_{s\\to 1}‖f(s)‖,$ if $f(s)=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5-s} \\\\ \\frac{{e}^{1-s}}{s} \\\\ (1+5s)^{1-s}\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{s\\to 1}f(s)=[\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 1}\\sqrt{5-s} \\\\ {lim}_{s\\to 1}\\frac{{e}^{1-s}}{1-s} \\\\ {lim}_{s\\to 1}\\,(1+5s)^{1/(2s)}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we find the limits one by one.\n\n- For the first component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 1}\\sqrt{5-s} & =\\sqrt{5-1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 1}\\frac{{e}^{1-s}}{s}=\\frac{1}{1}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the third component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 1}\\,(1+5s)^{1-s} & =(1+5\\cdot 1)^{1-1}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{s\\to 1}f(s)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, the limit of $‖f(s)‖$ as $s$ approaches $1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 1}‖f(s)‖ & =‖{lim}_{s\\to 1}f(s)‖ \\\\  & =‖[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563752 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115387 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "610e605b-30f6-574b-b149-3717cfd4d72a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Limit of the Magnitude of a Vector Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d97c90b-cd25-5463-946f-99b8a6ec2eec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563121} {:answer/id #uuid "6b1e462f-0fdb-5ac8-9d5a-a2cd343788a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563191} {:answer/id #uuid "7b02dac2-3766-5b1d-ac19-4a68e0d2e58c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563213} {:answer/id #uuid "da5b2088-8a89-5d89-85f1-998f57543e12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563422} {:answer/id #uuid "e71055d1-1a13-57e4-884a-be0ba2d1be55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563455}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da5b2088-8a89-5d89-85f1-998f57543e12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563422} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e315895-d72c-57a7-afdc-8b9e80c82011" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563538}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e2503fc5-32a5-54fb-be4e-1b9923b33c22" :question/math-academy-id "q-130214" :question/problem "Find the limit $\\,{lim}_{t\\to 0}‖f(t)‖,$ if $f(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+(t+2)^{2}\\,k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{t\\to 0}f(t)=({lim}_{t\\to 0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)i+({lim}_{t\\to 0}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)j+({lim}_{t\\to 0}(t+2)^{2})k.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the limits one by one.\n\n- For the first component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}\\operatorname{cos}⁡0=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the third component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}\\,(t+2)^{2} & =(0+2)^{2}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{t\\to 0}f(t)=j+4\\,k.$\n\nFinally, the limit of $‖f(t)‖$ as $t$ approaches $0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}‖f(t)‖ & =‖{lim}_{t\\to 0}f(t)‖ \\\\  & =‖j+4\\,k‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{17}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563663 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115388 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "68832b12-c34c-5770-9566-fc2fa915d005" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Limit of a Sum of Vector Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25f2c083-595e-5fcf-8705-992e3499809e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563032} {:answer/id #uuid "aadcbce8-c359-50f5-aca1-5c3b876cfa99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563330} {:answer/id #uuid "ac2ab553-7e7d-50fd-b187-d9032a06e4bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563333} {:answer/id #uuid "b85451f7-8926-5daf-a871-fbd1b79aa49e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563350} {:answer/id #uuid "f15462a2-749c-5944-bb07-7d5e7d74d1ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563484}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25f2c083-595e-5fcf-8705-992e3499809e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563032} :answer-field/id #uuid "7abde80b-69ef-507f-b94f-bbbd90c33e11" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563580}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2e0611fa-e2b7-5168-b829-407939c6ea09" :question/math-academy-id "q-130314" :question/problem "Find ${lim}_{t\\to 0}[f(t)+4g(t)]$ given that $f(t)$ and $g(t)$ are defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{t} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{t}^{2}+9}{t+3}\\end{aligned}],\\,g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}t-2 \\\\ \\frac{3t-2}{{t}^{2}-1} \\\\ {2}^{t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the limit of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}f(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}3{e}^{t} \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 0}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{{t}^{2}+9}{t+3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{0} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡0 \\\\ \\frac{{0}^{2}+9}{0+3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 0}g(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}\\,(t-2) \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{3t-2}{{t}^{2}-1} \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 0}{2}^{t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0-2 \\\\ \\frac{3(0)-2}{{0}^{2}-1} \\\\ {2}^{0}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use properties of limits to calculate the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}[f(t)+4g(t)] & ={lim}_{t\\to 0}f(t)+4{lim}_{t\\to 0}g(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+4[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563751 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115389 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb0058fd-f8c2-5f5d-bd48-f497537622dd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Limit of a Product of Vector Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "374e28b1-9d60-5567-9006-2366cebd20ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563068} {:answer/id #uuid "67f4a994-694a-52fa-9687-ee0e3b608236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563185} {:answer/id #uuid "7247832d-b063-5bbc-a125-48edef9b555a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563200} {:answer/id #uuid "76d89423-c5cf-587f-afc3-f3c4191d18a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563207} {:answer/id #uuid "bc1fe512-d096-5581-975f-b0f625e130b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67f4a994-694a-52fa-9687-ee0e3b608236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563185} :answer-field/id #uuid "df762a5a-9fee-5f06-a818-ced60d8cdc38" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563631}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e00ec48a-b851-58e1-a999-f80b28436a4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-130317" :question/problem "Find the limit ${lim}_{t\\to 0}[f(t)\\cdot g(t)]$ given that $f(t)$ and $g(t)$ are defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{t} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{t}^{2}+9}{t+3}\\end{aligned}],\\,g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}t-2 \\\\ \\frac{3t-2}{{t}^{2}-1} \\\\ {2}^{t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the limit of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}f(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}3{e}^{t} \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 0}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{{t}^{2}+9}{t+3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{0} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡0 \\\\ \\frac{{0}^{2}+9}{0+3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 0}g(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}\\,(t-2) \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{3t-2}{{t}^{2}-1} \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 0}{2}^{t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0-2 \\\\ \\frac{3(0)-2}{{0}^{2}-1} \\\\ {2}^{0}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use properties of limits to calculate the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}[f(t)\\cdot g(t)] & ={lim}_{t\\to 0}f(t)\\cdot {lim}_{t\\to 0}g(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =3(-2)+0(2)+3(1) \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563729 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115389 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb0058fd-f8c2-5f5d-bd48-f497537622dd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Limit of a Product of Vector Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37a1710a-45e4-557c-9442-1e74ba9112ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-18,12,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563069} {:answer/id #uuid "3f8fd679-95eb-5199-ba6a-a1cfb67ca9ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12,8,9⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563089} {:answer/id #uuid "7eacfd82-115e-5369-9ea0-e0661e38dc5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-12,18,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563222} {:answer/id #uuid "bbc42210-6e93-5e95-b495-30f65a2b1ba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,2,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563357} {:answer/id #uuid "e9e869f0-043f-53a7-9d36-e47ddd23102f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,8,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7eacfd82-115e-5369-9ea0-e0661e38dc5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-12,18,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563222} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a9c7ac2-4c78-5bd6-ac32-375910d4abbb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563562}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bd1d10fc-2d48-5d8e-aa22-57b49e0e6a49" :question/math-academy-id "q-130321" :question/problem "Find ${lim}_{t\\to 2}[f(t)\\times g(t)]$ given that $f(t)$ and $g(t)$ are defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨6-{t}^{3},\\,{t}^{2}-6,\\,\\frac{16}{{t}^{3}}⟩, \\\\ g(t) & =⟨5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3-t),\\,\\sqrt{6-t},\\,2t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the limit of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 2}f(t) & =⟨{lim}_{t\\to 2}\\,(6-{t}^{3}),\\,{lim}_{t\\to 2}\\,({t}^{2}-6),\\,{lim}_{t\\to 2}\\frac{16}{{t}^{3}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6-{2}^{3},{2}^{2}-6,\\frac{16}{{2}^{3}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,-2,2⟩ \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 2}g(t) & =⟨{lim}_{t\\to 2}\\,(5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3-t)),\\,{lim}_{t\\to 2}\\,\\sqrt{6-t},\\,{lim}_{t\\to 2}\\,2t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3-2),\\sqrt{6-2},2(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,2,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use properties of limits to calculate the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 2}[f(t)\\times g(t)] & ={lim}_{t\\to 2}f(t)\\times {lim}_{t\\to 2}g(t) \\\\  & =⟨-2,-2,2⟩\\times ⟨5,2,4⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot 4-2\\cdot 2)\\,i-((-2)\\cdot 4-5\\cdot 2)\\,j+((-2)\\cdot 2-5\\cdot (-2))\\,k \\\\  & =-12\\,i+18\\,j+6\\,k \\\\  & =⟨-12,18,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115757 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115388 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "68832b12-c34c-5770-9566-fc2fa915d005" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Limit of a Sum of Vector Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32f93cd8-2b18-5b9c-aa26-87db0d6e56ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨9,13,9⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563061} {:answer/id #uuid "37bbc342-deb2-5c62-b5f4-4c2ab96ccd4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨13,9,13⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563070} {:answer/id #uuid "4bbf07ed-8d8c-58e9-8f86-748f6bc62fb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8,4,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563111} {:answer/id #uuid "662e9f3a-b518-5488-a346-0c63d5a3acbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8,8,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563180} {:answer/id #uuid "c0e423a8-fc07-5848-a11c-d74f2340c97d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,5,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563369}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37bbc342-deb2-5c62-b5f4-4c2ab96ccd4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨13,9,13⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563070} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2571b8d-0d26-528a-b57d-8d0b05516a9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113508}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0780b7fe-8d13-5962-ac35-c60c83491b4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-32270" :question/problem "Find ${lim}_{t\\to 1}[5f(t)+2g(t)]$ given that $f(t)$ and $g(t)$ are defined as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨{t}^{2},{t}^{3},\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩ \\\\ g(t) & =⟨5-{t}^{3},{t}^{2}-t+2,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the limit of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}f(t) & =⟨{lim}_{t\\to 1}({t}^{2}),\\,{lim}_{t\\to 1}({t}^{3}),\\,{lim}_{t\\to 1}(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{1}^{2},{1}^{3},\\frac{1}{{1}^{2}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,1,1⟩ \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 1}g(t) & =⟨{lim}_{t\\to 1}(5-{t}^{3}),\\,{lim}_{t\\to 1}({t}^{2}-t+2),\\,{lim}_{t\\to 1}(4)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5-{1}^{3},{1}^{2}-1+2,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,2,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use properties of limits to calculate the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}[5f(t)+2g(t)] & ={lim}_{t\\to 1}5f(t)+{lim}_{t\\to 1}2g(t) \\\\  & =5{lim}_{t\\to 1}f(t)+2{lim}_{t\\to 1}g(t) \\\\  & =5⟨1,1,1⟩+2⟨4,2,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,5,5⟩+⟨8,4,8⟩ \\\\  & =⟨13,9,13⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115759 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115389 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb0058fd-f8c2-5f5d-bd48-f497537622dd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Limit of a Product of Vector Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c61cbc81-64a3-5a0e-b2b4-51f0e5c22c3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113521} {:answer/id #uuid "ea9fecc2-e570-5090-90de-e3bb4487e406" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113522} {:answer/id #uuid "2da9be63-1670-5830-8313-8546a9b933c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113523} {:answer/id #uuid "2f76f4a3-528b-592d-82ee-a243380cb31d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113524} {:answer/id #uuid "7506d646-9781-563c-851b-b6923974cad5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113525}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2da9be63-1670-5830-8313-8546a9b933c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113523} :answer-field/id #uuid "22775fac-83c5-5ccc-8957-14d77e8ce237" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113520}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "23598e85-48e6-53c4-b73f-532f246bbf47" :question/math-academy-id "q-32274" :question/problem "Find the limit ${lim}_{t\\to \\pi }[f(t)\\cdot g(t)]$ given that $f(t)$ and $g(t)$ are defined as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{4t}{\\pi }\\end{aligned}],\\,g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2+\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the limit of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\pi }f(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\pi }\\,(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to \\pi }\\,(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to \\pi }\\,(\\frac{4t}{\\pi })\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi  \\\\ 1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{4\\pi }{\\pi }\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to \\pi }g(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\pi }\\,(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to \\pi }\\,(2+\\operatorname{tan}⁡t) \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to \\pi }\\,(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi  \\\\ (2+\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\pi ) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi \\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use properties of limits to calculate the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\pi }[f(t)\\cdot g(t)] & ={lim}_{t\\to \\pi }f(t)\\cdot {lim}_{t\\to \\pi }g(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =0\\cdot (-1)+0\\cdot 2+4\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115774 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115388 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "68832b12-c34c-5770-9566-fc2fa915d005" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Limit of a Sum of Vector Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0e55031-dfcb-58bc-8ad8-dcd2b37f1f2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,-\\sqrt{2},-11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113611} {:answer/id #uuid "56467ebe-c7a2-586e-bb58-a5a7db3a157b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,-6,-9⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113614} {:answer/id #uuid "7cd4211b-e621-58bc-80fd-e9a6165b6884" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,6,11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563219} {:answer/id #uuid "dead4f12-ca88-5ad3-a931-528e8d88c330" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,6+\\sqrt{2},11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563433} {:answer/id #uuid "e79ae4b9-769d-5736-8cb4-dfec47ef6427" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,-6-\\sqrt{2},-11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e79ae4b9-769d-5736-8cb4-dfec47ef6427" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,-6-\\sqrt{2},-11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563462} :answer-field/id #uuid "e10a875d-c5bb-5531-8b0a-fc52f08b4474" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113610}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "94647436-6c02-573c-afcc-f91bf56c72c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-32973" :question/problem "Find ${lim}_{t\\to 0}[3f(t)-g(t)]$ given that\n$f(t)$ and $g(t)$ are defined as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,{t}^{2}-2,\\frac{t-3}{{t}^{2}+1}⟩ \\\\ g(t) & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\sqrt{t}+\\sqrt{2},2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the limit of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}f(t) & =⟨{lim}_{t\\to 0}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,{lim}_{t\\to 0}({t}^{2}-2),\\,{lim}_{t\\to 0}(\\frac{t-3}{{t}^{2}+1})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡0,{0}^{2}-2,\\frac{0-3}{{0}^{2}+1}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-2,-3⟩ \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 0}g(t) & =⟨{lim}_{t\\to 0}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,{lim}_{t\\to 0}(\\sqrt{t}+\\sqrt{2}),\\,{lim}_{t\\to 0}(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡0,\\sqrt{0}+\\sqrt{2},2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\sqrt{2},2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use properties of limits to calculate the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}[3f(t)-g(t)] & ={lim}_{t\\to 0}3f(t)-{lim}_{t\\to 0}g(t) \\\\  & =3{lim}_{t\\to 0}f(t)-{lim}_{t\\to 0}g(t) \\\\  & =3⟨1,-2,-3⟩-⟨0,\\sqrt{2},2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-6,-9⟩-⟨0,\\sqrt{2},2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3-0,-6-\\sqrt{2},-9-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-6-\\sqrt{2},-11⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563716 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115387 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "610e605b-30f6-574b-b149-3717cfd4d72a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Limit of the Magnitude of a Vector Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "206b7aff-d2d1-5f6a-add6-b653f58dc164" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563018} {:answer/id #uuid "60f53833-01a7-51b3-b367-c22fe50326ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563170} {:answer/id #uuid "a0d74bba-4689-5ebb-920d-944005be742c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563307} {:answer/id #uuid "c5495620-9d83-5275-9d56-bcfc0407808d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563379} {:answer/id #uuid "e0f6b4d0-5d37-52d1-8795-c9a0b9d298d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563441}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5495620-9d83-5275-9d56-bcfc0407808d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563379} :answer-field/id #uuid "a738fbe9-b746-555f-a431-6ff37c754328" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563610}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9a567a48-e070-587a-94df-8a2d7148a763" :question/math-academy-id "q-32976" :question/problem "Calculate ${lim}_{s\\to 0}‖f(s)‖$, if $f(s)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{s}{(s+1)^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡s}{{s}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡s}{2{s}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]\\,.$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall that:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 0}f(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 0}\\frac{s}{(s+1)^{2}} \\\\ {lim}_{s\\to 0}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡s}{{s}^{2}} \\\\ {lim}_{s\\to 0}\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡s}{2{s}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the limits one-by-one.\n\n- For the first component, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 0}\\frac{s}{(s+1)^{2}} & =\\frac{0}{(0+1)^{2}}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second component can be found using a special limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 0}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡s}{{s}^{2}} & ={lim}_{s\\to 0}{(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡s}{s})}^{2} \\\\  & ={({lim}_{s\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡s}{s})}^{2} \\\\  & ={1}^{2} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third component can be found using L'Hopital's Rule twice:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 0}\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡s}{2{s}^{2}} & ={lim}_{s\\to 0}\\frac{{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡s)}^{″}}{{(2{s}^{2})}^{″}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{s\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡s}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡0}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{s\\to 0}f(s)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1/4\\end{aligned}]\\,.$\n\nFinally, the limit of $‖f(s)‖$ as $s$ approaches $0$ is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 0}‖f(s)‖ & =‖{lim}_{s\\to 0}f(s)‖ \\\\  & =‖[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1/4\\end{aligned}]‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563662 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115387 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "610e605b-30f6-574b-b149-3717cfd4d72a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Limit of the Magnitude of a Vector Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4696a05b-aa71-5436-909d-4ad6cc69953d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563104} {:answer/id #uuid "4d2524ac-5a9e-5166-a59a-c4b1cc71b052" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{41}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563116} {:answer/id #uuid "830ff5aa-499a-5e23-8b6c-9f66271ff7d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{39}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563237} {:answer/id #uuid "d146c1fe-0d81-525c-ab3e-04de8c098617" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{39}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563404} {:answer/id #uuid "e4967a7e-ba74-5964-80d2-08e8ecb2bbc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{41}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563447}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4967a7e-ba74-5964-80d2-08e8ecb2bbc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{41}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563447} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1f9bfc4-206c-5615-9e86-3cd20425df2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563627}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2cd66931-0513-5d1c-9823-4729248ee301" :question/math-academy-id "q-32979" :question/problem "Find the limit ${lim}_{t\\to 1}‖f(t)‖$, if $f(t)=\\frac{4+t}{5}\\,i+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1)}{{t}^{2}-1}\\,j+\\sqrt{9t}\\,k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall that:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}f(t) & =({lim}_{t\\to 1}\\frac{4+t}{5})\\,i+({lim}_{t\\to 1}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1)}{{t}^{2}-1})\\,j+({lim}_{t\\to 1}\\sqrt{9t})\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the limits one-by-one.\n\n- For the first component, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}\\frac{4+t}{5} & =\\frac{4+1}{5}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second component can be found using a special limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1)}{{t}^{2}-1} & ={lim}_{t\\to 1}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1)}{(t-1)(t+1)} \\\\  & =({lim}_{t\\to 1}\\frac{1}{t+1})\\cdot ({lim}_{t\\to 1}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1)}{t-1}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{1+1})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the third component, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}\\sqrt{9t} & =\\sqrt{9(1)}=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{t\\to 1}f(t)=i+\\frac{1}{2}\\,j+3\\,k.$\n\nFinally, the limit of $‖f(t)‖$ as $t$ approaches $1$ is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}‖f(t)‖ & =‖{lim}_{t\\to 1}f(t)‖ \\\\  & =‖i+\\frac{1}{2}\\,j+3\\,k‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{4}+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{41}{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{41}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563667 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115386 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ac33006-2d6d-5ee2-9749-a1f3dea17869" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Limit of a Vector Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16f9d3ac-e7ee-5e21-82c1-471755a55162" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ e\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562996} {:answer/id #uuid "3d7dcd81-555d-55d1-a1bb-f7eb9aaa9c08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ e\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563083} {:answer/id #uuid "58c3f0b4-edb0-5ecc-b12a-48bd5b853604" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1 \\\\ e\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563143} {:answer/id #uuid "e71f20cb-af6e-5fbd-8e27-40edcce524cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563456} {:answer/id #uuid "fbb22881-51b2-5948-adba-093b2535b458" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ e \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58c3f0b4-edb0-5ecc-b12a-48bd5b853604" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1 \\\\ e\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563143} :answer-field/id #uuid "84218ae0-ac5d-5acd-ba70-5324cc9dc6e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563585}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "37a31447-f0c5-5a53-afc7-a1edb4864b07" :question/math-academy-id "q-32987" :question/problem "Calculate ${lim}_{s\\to 0}f(s)$, if $f(s)=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{s+8} \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡s}{s} \\\\ (1+2s)^{1/(2s)}\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall that:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{s\\to 0}f(s)=[\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 0}\\sqrt{s+8} \\\\ {lim}_{s\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡s}{s} \\\\ {lim}_{s\\to 0}(1+2s)^{1/(2s)}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we find the limits one-by-one.\n\n- For the first component, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 0}\\sqrt{s+8} & =\\sqrt{0+8} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{3}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second component can be found using L'Hopital's Rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡s}{s} & ={lim}_{s\\to 0}\\frac{{(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡s)}^{′}}{{s}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{s\\to 0}\\frac{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{s}^{2}}}}{1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{s\\to 0}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{s}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third component can be found using a special limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 0}(1+2s)^{1/(2s)} & ={lim}_{u\\to 0}(1+u)^{1/u}=e\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{s\\to 0}f(s)=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1 \\\\ e\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563712 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115387 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "610e605b-30f6-574b-b149-3717cfd4d72a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Limit of the Magnitude of a Vector Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2100df4f-3a3b-55cc-a852-f5c980aced39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563019} {:answer/id #uuid "343f0047-5e45-5525-a95d-3d82e6459514" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563063} {:answer/id #uuid "94d0189d-b6e8-5ec0-91a7-24c6aa1126d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563276} {:answer/id #uuid "c8baf397-fb31-54b6-9eeb-ba95d1df79e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563387} {:answer/id #uuid "cb7e9cb6-5c59-5664-9b12-adadc37bf320" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563396}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "343f0047-5e45-5525-a95d-3d82e6459514" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563063} :answer-field/id #uuid "c84f65d5-7aae-5814-8581-c9fd5f811b31" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563623}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "86cd099b-e0a6-5dec-b63e-d3e60dda2214" :question/math-academy-id "q-69728" :question/problem "Calculate ${lim}_{t\\to 3}‖f(t)‖$, if $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}-3t \\\\ \\frac{1}{{t}^{2}-8} \\\\ 5-2t\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall that:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{t\\to 3}f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 3}({t}^{2}-3t) \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 3}\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}-8} \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 3}(5-2t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we find the limits one-by-one.\n\n- For the first component, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 3}({t}^{2}-3t) & ={3}^{2}-3(3)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second component, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 3}\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}-8} & =\\frac{1}{{3}^{2}-8}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the third component, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 3}(5-2t) & =5-2(3)=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{t\\to 3}f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, the limit of $‖f(t)‖$ as $t$ approaches $3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 3}‖f(t)‖ & =‖{lim}_{t\\to 3}f(t)‖ \\\\  & =‖[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563727 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115388 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "68832b12-c34c-5770-9566-fc2fa915d005" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Limit of a Sum of Vector Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0df3defd-3254-5256-8de1-8bab9ab5c062" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562970} {:answer/id #uuid "2e1b88bd-51e6-5eb2-949f-71b11846824d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563048} {:answer/id #uuid "78285f75-cb3b-5911-b998-4b1257c89e6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563210} {:answer/id #uuid "7b8c9926-eedb-56f1-bea0-3e8216b12c98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563214} {:answer/id #uuid "d51fe666-cdc2-5a8b-9abc-7c4c02e5d063" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e1b88bd-51e6-5eb2-949f-71b11846824d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563048} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a9b9373-bdb4-5460-8dab-9626078627ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563535}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b9ad6ae2-908f-5e67-9c92-f2b932e8cd1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-69730" :question/problem "Find ${lim}_{t\\to 0}[f(t)+g(t)]$ given that $f(t)$ and $g(t)$ are defined as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} \\\\ {e}^{t} \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{t}\\end{aligned}],\\,g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 1 \\\\ \\frac{2t-1}{{t}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the limit of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}{t}^{2} \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 0}{e}^{t} \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{0}^{2} \\\\ {e}^{0} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the third component is a special limit.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 0}1 \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{2t-1}{{t}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ \\frac{2(0)-1}{{0}^{2}+1})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use properties of limits to calculate the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}[f(t)+g(t)] & ={lim}_{t\\to 0}f(t)+{lim}_{t\\to 0}g(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563706 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115388 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "68832b12-c34c-5770-9566-fc2fa915d005" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Limit of a Sum of Vector Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "197c2f63-1083-5901-8e61-bfcf01463d0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2j+e\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563004} {:answer/id #uuid "6f8f006f-3832-5387-87b5-aeddea710ee9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+2j+e\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563196} {:answer/id #uuid "71e370b0-a033-516b-ac92-3d2a5f4e8fe2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2i+j+(e+2)\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563199} {:answer/id #uuid "917a3dde-c5a6-52e4-a99f-41cfccafc5ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3i+2j+e\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563270} {:answer/id #uuid "b5a29a28-e998-5dd3-a0ec-234ddb1be820" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+(e+2)\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "197c2f63-1083-5901-8e61-bfcf01463d0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2j+e\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563004} :answer-field/id #uuid "f149eee6-2250-502c-8bd6-58d081055e65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563636}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7d74654a-36dd-50ce-be7e-dc0c748c4dcb" :question/math-academy-id "q-69736" :question/problem "Find ${lim}_{t\\to \\infty }[g(t)+2f(t)]$ given that $f(t)$ and $g(t)$ are defined as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =\\frac{{t}^{2}}{1-{t}^{2}}\\,i+(1+\\frac{1}{t})\\,j+{t}^{-2}\\,k \\\\ g(t) & =2\\,i+{e}^{-t}\\,j+{(1+\\frac{1}{t})}^{t}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the limit of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }f(t) & =({lim}_{t\\to \\infty }\\frac{{t}^{2}}{1-{t}^{2}})\\,i+({lim}_{t\\to \\infty }(1+\\frac{1}{t}))\\,j-({lim}_{t\\to \\infty }{t}^{-2})\\,k, \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to \\infty }g(t) & =({lim}_{t\\to \\infty }2)\\,i-({lim}_{t\\to \\infty }{e}^{-t})\\,j+({lim}_{t\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{t})}^{t})\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's find the limits one-by-one.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {lim}_{t\\to \\infty }\\frac{{t}^{2}}{1-{t}^{2}}={lim}_{t\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}-1}=-1 \\\\  & {lim}_{t\\to \\infty }(1+\\frac{1}{t})=1+{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{t}=1 \\\\  & {lim}_{t\\to \\infty }{t}^{-2}={lim}_{t\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}=0 \\\\  & {lim}_{t\\to \\infty }2=2 \\\\  & {lim}_{t\\to \\infty }{e}^{-t}=0 \\\\  & {lim}_{t\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{t})}^{t}=e\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }f(t) & =-1\\,i+1\\,j+0\\,k \\\\  & =-i+j, \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to \\infty }g(t) & =2\\,i+0\\,j+e\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,i+e\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use properties of limits to calculate the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }[g(t)+2f(t)] & ={lim}_{t\\to \\infty }g(t)+2{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }f(t) \\\\  & =(2\\,i+e\\,k)+2(-i+j) \\\\  & =2j+e\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563664 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115389 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb0058fd-f8c2-5f5d-bd48-f497537622dd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Limit of a Product of Vector Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e7082bf-94bc-5f95-a646-926615cd1b1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-{e}^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563123} {:answer/id #uuid "5f6847e3-eb2c-5cc6-9cd0-83733cfef02d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563164} {:answer/id #uuid "873d5f29-f5c3-5d96-8997-2e96d20efdab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563247} {:answer/id #uuid "8ccbdb14-9c0c-5f46-a3d4-ae2fd1da959c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563262} {:answer/id #uuid "920aaecc-64b5-5927-be63-43fbf263f51a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563271}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "873d5f29-f5c3-5d96-8997-2e96d20efdab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563247} :answer-field/id #uuid "b24006f7-dcb6-5a3e-962f-d3babb6d995e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563615}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "33768c70-a4a8-56c5-b929-58df88c6ba1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-78268" :question/problem "Find the limit ${lim}_{t\\to 1}[f(t)\\cdot g(t)]$ given that $f(t)$ and $g(t)$ are defined as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{t-1} \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t}{t} \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t}{t}\\end{aligned}],\\,g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{t}^{2}-2t+1}{t+1} \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+t}{t+1} \\\\ \\frac{{e}^{t+1}}{t+1}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the limit of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}f(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}\\,(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{t-1}) \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 1}\\,(\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t}{t}) \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 1}\\,(\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t}{t})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}\\,(\\frac{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)^{′}}{(t-1)^{′}}) \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 1}\\,(\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t}{t}) \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 1}\\,(\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t}{t})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}\\,(\\frac{1}{t}) \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi }{1} \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi }{1}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that for the first component of ${lim}_{t\\to 1}f(t)$ we used L'Hopital's Rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}g(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}\\,\\frac{{t}^{2}-2t+1}{t+1} \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 1}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+t}{t+1} \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 1}\\,\\frac{{e}^{t+1}}{t+1}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{1}^{2}-2\\cdot 1+1}{1+1} \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+1}{1+1} \\\\ \\frac{{e}^{1+1}}{1+1}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use properties of limits to calculate the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}[f(t)\\cdot g(t)] & ={lim}_{t\\to 1}f(t)\\cdot {lim}_{t\\to 1}g(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0+(-2)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+0\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{2}}{2} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563649 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115389 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb0058fd-f8c2-5f5d-bd48-f497537622dd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Limit of a Product of Vector Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e7b3ee8-302c-5bb1-a016-50116576c2f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562973} {:answer/id #uuid "7f679746-4683-54bf-906e-e3418d6fd20d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563226} {:answer/id #uuid "9a621fae-e013-5531-ad51-a186fffabdb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563294} {:answer/id #uuid "a18cb561-1016-5b60-a141-a208ee290e53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563309} {:answer/id #uuid "dfc4555a-8d25-52bb-84f7-9a18b8237849" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563436}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfc4555a-8d25-52bb-84f7-9a18b8237849" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563436} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa331f7b-2a1a-5cc2-9b0b-49206016e7e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563639}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0e9c7e83-813e-5902-881b-22d16eab32e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-78269" :question/problem "Find the limit ${lim}_{t\\to 0}[f(t)\\cdot g(t)]$ given that $f(t)$ and $g(t)$ are defined as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨\\frac{{t}^{2}-2t+2}{t+1},\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)}{t},\\,t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ g(t) & =⟨\\frac{{e}^{2t}-1}{t},\\,1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,t+1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the limit of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}f(t) & =⟨{lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{{t}^{2}-2t+2}{t+1},\\,{lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)}{t},\\,{lim}_{t\\to 0}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{{t}^{2}-2t+2}{t+1},\\,2{lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)}{(2t)},\\,{lim}_{t\\to 0}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{{0}^{2}-2\\cdot 0+2}{0+1},\\,2\\cdot 1,\\,0\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,2,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that for the second component of ${lim}_{t\\to 0}f(t)$ we used a special limit ${lim}_{u\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡u}{u}=1.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}g(t) & =⟨{lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{2t}-1}{t},\\,{lim}_{t\\to 0}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,{lim}_{t\\to 0}(t+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{({e}^{2t}-1)^{′}}{(t)^{′}},\\,{lim}_{t\\to 0}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,{lim}_{t\\to 0}(t+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{2{e}^{2t}}{1},\\,{lim}_{t\\to 0}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,{lim}_{t\\to 0}(t+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{0},\\,1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0,\\,0+1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,0,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that for the first component of ${lim}_{t\\to 0}g(t)$ we used L'Hopital's Rule.\n\nNow, we use properties of limits to calculate the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}[f(t)\\cdot g(t)] & ={lim}_{t\\to 0}f(t)\\cdot {lim}_{t\\to 0}g(t) \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,2,\\,0⟩\\cdot ⟨2,0,1⟩ \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
